# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Content-Security-Policy is in Report-Only mode: nothing is blocked, the
# browser only logs violations to the DevTools console. Once a week of normal
# use shows no violations (GA4, Google Ads call tracking, Clarity after
# consent, the booking form), rename the header to Content-Security-Policy to
# enforce it.
#
# script-src allows the inline scripts by sha256 hash: the GA4/Ads block in
# every <head> and each page's language-toggle script (they differ slightly
# between pages, hence several hashes). 'unsafe-hashes' plus the last two
# hashes allow the onclick="setLang('cs')" / onclick="setLang('en')" buttons.
# Editing any inline script changes its hash - DevTools prints the expected
# value in the violation message; add it here or the script will be blocked
# once the policy is enforced.
#
# Google Ads call tracking needs googleadservices, doubleclick and the Google
# country domain the visitor lands on (www.google.cz for Czech visitors).
# The Apps Script form endpoint redirects to script.googleusercontent.com.
# frame-src www.google.com is the click-to-load homepage map (main.js).

